        <text class="dim-text" x="168" y="52">R90</text>
        <text class="dim-text" x="168" y="180">⌀28</text>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- =========================================================
     ABOUT
     ========================================================= -->
<section id="about">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>About</h2>
      <span class="section-num">§ 01</span>
    </div>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-photo"></div>
      <div class="about-text">
        <p>Hi, I'm Haven Dao, a mechanical engineer currently attending Palomar College. Welcome to my website.
        <p>I'm a mechanical engineer focused on <strong>robotics, mechanism design, and rapid prototyping</strong>. I like problems that live at the boundary of mechanical, electrical, and software systems — where a good linkage design and a good control loop both matter.</p>
        <p>Most recently I've been working on actuated mechanisms and small autonomous platforms, taking each from early sketches through SolidWorks, simulation, machining, and on-bench testing. I'm comfortable running a project end to end: spec it, design it, build it, break it, fix it.</p>
        <p>Outside of coursework and personal builds, I've spent time in a machine shop and on a small robotics team, which is where most of my instincts about tolerancing and failure modes actually came from.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- =========================================================
     PROJECTS
     ========================================================= -->
<section id="work" class="projects">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Selected work</h2>
      <p class="section-note">Each project below covers the problem, the approach, and where it ended up — with links to the repo or full write-up.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Project 1 -->
    <article class="project-sheet">
      <div class="project-media">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 260 200">
          <rect x="40" y="60" width="180" height="90" rx="2"/>
          <line x1="60" y1="60" x2="60" y2="30"/>
          <line x1="200" y1="60" x2="200" y2="30"/>
